* [cite_start]**The Work**: The Original Work or its Derivative Works[cite: 52].
* [cite_start]**The Source Code**: The human-readable form of the Work which is the most convenient for people to study and modify[cite: 53].
* [cite_start]**The Executable Code**: Any code which has generally been compiled and meant to be interpreted by a computer[cite: 54].
* [cite_start]**The Licensor**: The natural or legal person that distributes or communicates the Work under the Licence[cite: 55].
* [cite_start]**Contributor(s)**: Any natural or legal person who modifies the Work under the Licence[cite: 56].
* [cite_start]**The Licensee ('You')**: Any natural or legal person who makes any usage of the Work under the terms of the Licence[cite: 57].
* [cite_start]**Distribution or Communication**: Any act of selling, giving, lending, renting, distributing, communicating, transmitting, or otherwise making available the Work[cite: 58, 59].

